---
title: Atbash cipher
tags: tools
summary: >-
    Swaps each letter for its mirror image in the alphabet, so <code class="tool-example">A ↔ Z</code> and <code class="tool-example">B ↔ Y</code>.
---
{% from "macros/tool.njk" import toolSection with context %}
{% from "macros/tool-frame.njk" import toolFrame %}
{% set filename = page.fileSlug %}
{% set intro %}
    <p>A simple substitution cipher: each letter swaps with the one the same distance from the other end of the alphabet, so <code class="tool-example">C ↔ X</code>, <code class="tool-example">D ↔ W</code> and so on.</p>
    <p>More on the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Atbash" class="text-convrtr">Atbash</a> Wikipedia page.</p>
{% endset %}
{% call toolSection(intro) %}
{% call toolFrame(filename, "Atbash cipher", placeholder = "Example: (Hello &lrarr; Svool)") %}
<div class="input-group w-auto">
    <button class="btn btn-convrtr" type="button" id="{{ filename }}Encrypt">Encrypt</button>
</div>
{% endcall %}
{% endcall %}
